The error points to the statement `l_batch.EXTEND;` in the selected function, which is line 5 of the supplied source:

```text
FUNCTION first_batch RETURN NUMBER IS
  TYPE batch_t IS TABLE OF NUMBER;
  l_batch batch_t;
BEGIN
  l_batch.EXTEND;
  ...
```

`l_batch` is declared as a nested table collection, but it is not initialized. A PL/SQL collection variable declared this way is null until it is assigned an empty collection. Calling `EXTEND` on that null collection raises `ORA-06531: Reference to uninitialized collection`.

The supplied selection begins with a bare `FUNCTION` and no package context is shown, so the complete replacement below treats it as a standalone routine. The change initializes `l_batch` with the empty nested table constructor `batch_t()` before `EXTEND` is called. This replacement has not been compiled or run.

```plsql
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION first_batch RETURN NUMBER IS
  TYPE batch_t IS TABLE OF NUMBER;
  l_batch batch_t := batch_t();
BEGIN
  l_batch.EXTEND;
  l_batch(1) := 17;
  RETURN l_batch(1);
END first_batch;
```

